From 63ed033990caeadf6508b4061d85137107d2eb5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:20:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: use thermal-engine's own MSM8917 configuration, as
 stock does

The first template shipped an MSM8937 thermal-engine.conf (8 cores, a
tsens 10 GPU sensor). On this 4-core MSM8917 its CPU loop drove the
cpu_voltage device and its skin loop cluster0, neither of which exists
here (the one cluster is cluster1; thermal-engine logs "Invalid dev
cluster0" and fails to add the CPU voltage device), so the CPUs were
never throttled for heat; it also hotplugged a CPU5, capped at 902 MHz
(no such step) and had no tsens 0-9 cold-voltage monitors in the right
set. Stock EMUI ships the file empty, so thermal-engine uses its
built-in MSM8917 configuration: CPUs at 85 C and the case at 44 C on
cluster1 (cap 960 MHz), GPU limits, charging control and cold-voltage
restriction on all ten tsens sensors. Ship stock's empty file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016iwHzV2tPonTxdceSkWZtS
---
 configs/thermal-engine.conf | 232 +-----------------------------------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 230 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configs/thermal-engine.conf b/configs/thermal-engine.conf
index 49968db..33fc821 100644
--- a/configs/thermal-engine.conf
+++ b/configs/thermal-engine.conf
@@ -1,230 +1,2 @@
